# The buried oxide is the thermal resistance to the substrate: a thicker one makes the shifter more efficient and slower.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Buried oxide 4 um thick
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=60 ymin=-10 ymax=7
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 7
rect si -0.25 0.25 4 4.25
rect tin -1 1 6 6.25
heater h xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=6 ymax=6.25 power=0.1
probe wg xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=4 ymax=4.25
expect response wg h 257.627743 1e-7
expect pi_power wg h 16.1732064 1e-7
expect peak 49.2416815 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 16320
